#### Major Issues Faced:

**❌ PROBLEM 7: TF Timestamp Extrapolation Errors**

**Error:**
```
[ERROR] Lookup would require extrapolation into the future.
Requested time 1772156192 but latest data is at time 33.851000
```

**Root Cause:** Vision nodes using **wall clock time** instead of **simulation time**
```
Vision timestamp: 1772156192 seconds (year 2026 real time!)
TF timestamp: 33.851000 seconds (33 sec simulation time)
→ MISMATCH! Cannot transform!

Why This Happened:

    ROS2 nodes default to system time
    Simulation uses /clock topic for sim time
    Nodes must explicitly declare use_sim_time parameter

Attempted Solutions:

    ❌ Adding self.declare_parameter('use_sim_time', True) in node
        Worked when using ros2 run, but...
    ❌ Launching with launch file that also sets parameter
        Caused "Parameter already declared" error!

Final Solution:
python

# In node __init__ - DON'T declare if using launch file
# Just use get_clock().now() which respects use_sim_time

# In launch file - Set parameter here:
Node(
    package='leo_lidar_sim',
    executable='detection_node.py',
    parameters=[{'use_sim_time': True}]  # ← Launch file sets it!
)
```

**Created:** `vision_system.launch.py` - Launches both vision nodes with correct time parameters

